🦀 Existing Rust Routers You Can Use
Here are the main ones:

Tool	What It Does	Why It Fits Syntropia
millwright	Routes requests based on cost tiers (cheap, mid, frontier)	Good for cost management
octoroute	Routes based on task complexity (simple → 8B, complex → 120B)	Good for smart task routing
oxllm	Super lightweight gateway (~2.6MB binary) with failover	Good for low-resource nodes
Ultrafast AI Gateway	Enterprise-grade, <1ms latency, 10K+ req/sec	Good for high-performance swarm
Aura LLM Gateway	Supports 9+ providers, unified API	Good for multi-provider setups
moaray	Multi-agent routing; can call multiple models in parallel	Good for swarm orchestration
✅ Why Rust Is Good for This
Benefit	What It Means
Fast	Microsecond latency, not milliseconds.
Memory-safe	No crashes from memory errors.
Lightweight	Small binary size (~2-5 MB).
Concurrent	Handles many requests at once.
Production-ready	These tools are already being used.
